From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:17:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mt6351: restore the charge pump configuration at
 power-down

The negative charge pump's configuration register is written at power-up
and only its enable bit is cleared at power-down, so it keeps 0x8c00
from then on. The vendor driver writes 0x4600 when it disables the pump.

Do the same. The register also reads 0x4600 before the first power-up.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/mt6351.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/mt6351.c b/sound/soc/codecs/mt6351.c
index 976770c..b539dc3 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/mt6351.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/mt6351.c
@@ -640,6 +640,11 @@ static int mt_ncp_event(struct snd_soc_dapm_widget *w,
 	case SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU:
 		usleep_range(250, 270);
 		break;
+	case SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMD:
+		/* the disabled configuration, as the vendor driver restores it */
+		regmap_update_bits(cmpnt->regmap, MT6351_AFE_NCP_CFG0,
+				   0xfffe, 0x4600);
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
@@ -1087,7 +1092,8 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget mt6351_dapm_widgets[] = {
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("NCP", MT6351_AFE_NCP_CFG0,
 			    RG_NCP_ON_BIT, 0,
 			    mt_ncp_event,
-			    SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU),
+			    SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU |
+			    SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMD),
 
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("DL Digital Clock", SND_SOC_NOPM,
 			    0, 0, NULL, 0),
